-- The same refusal as `export-refused.l4`, one hop further out: this module
-- imports `implicit-rate-wrapper`, which imports `implicit-rate-lib`, and only
-- the last of the three declares a section GIVEN.
--
-- An adversarial pass found this a false green on 2026-09-08, and a silent one:
-- `l4 batch --validate-only` said valid, the run said "status":"success", and
-- the answer was the library's own TYPICALLY with the supplied value accepted
-- into the row and dropped. The middle module contributes to what its importers
-- learn only because a definition that REACHES an imported reader is now itself
-- counted as one.

IMPORT `implicit-rate-wrapper`

@export What this amount comes to at a rate two modules away.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`chained cost of` amount MEANS `wrapped cost of` amount
